name: aggregate
description: >-
  An aggregate rule: every matching choice contributes to a list output,
  instead of the first match deciding. The compiler accepts it; the supported
  profile refuses it (celcheck's restricted-profile check), because only
  first-match has tests of its emitted CheckedExpr on every evaluator.
rule:
  aggregate:
    - condition: iteration == "commit"
      output: '"form_check"'
    - output: '"unknown"'
